e><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAO KAICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUGIHARA NORIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAKI, EIICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MANABE, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAO, KAICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIHARA, NORIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An aqueous polyamide resin dispersion comprising dispersed particles of a polyamide resin, a basic substance, and water. The dispersed polyamide resin particles have a weight-average particle diameter of 0.1 to 10  mu m. In the polyamide resin, the ratio of terminal carboxyl groups to terminal amino groups is 60/40 to 100/0. The amount of the basic substance is 0.2 to 3.0 mol per mol of the terminal carboxyl groups. This aqueous polyamide resin dispersion can be produced by adding a polyamide resin to an aqueous dispersion medium containing a basic substance in an amount of 0.2 to 3.0 mol per mol of the terminal carboxyl groups contained in the polyamide resin.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une dispersion de résine polyamide aqueuse renfermant des particules dispersées d'une résine polyamide, une substance basique et de l'eau. Les particules de résine polyamide dispersées ont un diamètre de particule de poids moyen de 0,1 à 10  mu m. Dans la résine polyamide, le taux des groupes carboxyles terminaux par rapport aux groupes amino terminaux est de 60/40 à 100/0. La quantité de substance basique est de 0,2 à 3,0 mol par mol de groupes carboxyles terminaux. On peut produire cette dispersion de résine polyamide aqueuse en ajoutant une résine polyamide à un milieu de dispersion aqueuse contenant une substance basique d'une quantité de 0,2 à 3,0 mol par mol des groupes carboxyles terminaux contenus dans la résine polyamide.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>